{"name":"Tiger Cat","hex":"#cda035","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tiger cat","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several species of felids.","A tiger quoll (Dasyurus maculatus). .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tiger_cat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oncilla","blocks":[{"text":"The oncilla, also known as the northern tiger cat, little spotted cat, and tigrillo, is a small spotted cat ranging from Central America to central Brazil. It is listed as Vulnerable on the IUCN Red List, and the population is threatened by deforestation and conversion of habitat to agricultural land."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Snethlage%27s_Tigrina_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_354017009_on_2_August_2024_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Snethlage%27s_Tigrina_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_354017009_on_2_August_2024_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oncilla","wikidata":"Q205948"},{"title":"Tiger","blocks":[{"text":"The tiger is a large cat and a member of the genus Panthera native to Asia. It has a powerful, muscular body with a large head and paws, a long tail and orange fur that fades to white in parts, with black, mostly vertical stripes. It is traditionally classified into nine subspecies, though some recognise only two subspecies, the mainland Asian tiger and the Sunda Islands tiger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Bengal_tiger_%28Panthera_tigris_tigris%29_female_3_crop.jpg/330px-Bengal_tiger_%28Panthera_tigris_tigris%29_female_3_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger","wikidata":"Q19939"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Snethlage%27s_Tigrina_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_354017009_on_2_August_2024_%